    {
      "id": "ES-C403-pollo",
      "sequence": 8950,
      "title": "el pollo — chicken, not dust",
      "headword": "el pollo",
      "romanization": "el pollo",
      "gloss": "chicken — the food word to keep distinct from polvo, dust",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:8ed0565103cf2024",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": -1,
          "type": "unknown",
          "title": "",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "<!-- Safety: teach pollo only against polvo. Do not generate polla/pollas, do not use echar near polvo, and do not turn this contrast into a gender drill. See HL24 section 6.2. The missing forms are deliberate. -->."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say the meat. (La carne.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "pronunciation",
          "title": "Sounds you'll need",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "PO-yo for most speakers: written ll commonly has the sound of English y. Keep the final vowel round and clear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "el pollo — “the chicken,” especially chicken as food."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Latin pullus meant a young animal. Spanish pollo comes from that word. Keep it distinct from polvo, “dust,” which comes from unrelated Latin pulvis. The useful listening contrast is only pollo / polvo: the first has -ll-, the second has -lv-."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "el pollo",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *el pollo*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "pollo, no polvo",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *pollo, no polvo*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "carne de pollo",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *carne de pollo*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say the chicken, then contrast it with dust. (El pollo; pollo, no polvo.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sources: DLE: pollo and DLE: polvo."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ES-C403-verdura",
      "sequence": 8960,
      "title": "la verdura — the green growth that became vegetables",
      "headword": "la verdura",
      "romanization": "la verdura",
      "gloss": "vegetables or greens — from verde, with a marked secondary sense outside this food use",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:d970dcffb3df93d0",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Name chicken and fruit. (El pollo, la fruta.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "pronunciation",
          "title": "Sounds you'll need",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ver-DU-ra: tap the single r once; the stress falls on du."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "la verdura — “the vegetables” or “the greens.”"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The word is built on verde, from Latin viridis, “green.” The food sense grew from green plant growth. But verde cannot be reduced to a colour in every context: Spanish can also use it of an indecent or erotic joke, and the dictionary records a marked secondary sense of verdura. Here the context is plainly food."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "la verdura",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *la verdura*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "fruta y verdura",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *fruta y verdura*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "pollo con verdura",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *pollo con verdura*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Give the supermarket pair: fruit and vegetables. (Fruta y verdura.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sources: DLE: verdura and DLE: verde."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ES-C403-paella",
      "sequence": 8970,
      "title": "la paella — the pan that named the dish",
      "headword": "la paella",
      "romanization": "la paella",
      "gloss": "paella — the Valencian rice dish named from the pan",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:38541cebc06aeba7",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say to cook and the vegetables. (Cocinar, la verdura.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "pronunciation",
          "title": "Sounds you'll need",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pa-E-ya for most speakers: keep three clear beats, with the stress on e."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "la paella — “paella,” the Valencian rice dish."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The dish took the name of its pan. Valencian paella came through Old French paele from Latin patella, a small pan or dish. Catalan also has native padella; the different middle consonant is evidence that paella made the French detour rather than wearing down inside Catalan."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "la paella",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *la paella*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "cocinar paella",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *cocinar paella*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "paella con pollo y verdura",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *paella con pollo y verdura*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say that your mother cooks paella. (Mi madre cocina paella.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Source: DLE: paella."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
